    "date": "2026-10-26 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-26 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2023 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-98432:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period\n\nCVE-2026-98384:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix out-of-bounds read of sk_protocol in bpf_sock_destroy()\n\nCVE-2026-98383:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Disallow bpf_skb_pull_data() for LWT_SEG6LOCAL\n\nCVE-2026-98382:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Reject dev-bound-only programs on other devices\n\nCVE-2026-98381:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nveth: manage XDP program pointers during channel resize\n\nCVE-2026-98380:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/sched: reject IDR error pointers when deleting actions\n\nCVE-2026-98379:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: ip6t_rpfilter: reject routes without inet6_dev\n\nCVE-2026-98378:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Skip unsettled links in link iterator\n\nCVE-2026-98377:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvlan: require the MAC header to be present in __vlan_insert_inner_tag()\n\nCVE-2026-98375:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxen/netfront: drop RX packets with a short Ethernet header\n\nCVE-2026-98374:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: fix use-after-free of retransmit_skb_hint in tcp_send_synack()\n\nCVE-2026-98373:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmm/hugetlb: preserve mremap address delta when skipping page tables\n\nCVE-2026-98364:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfrm: hold net_device reference under RCU in bundle creation\n\nCVE-2026-98084:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: backtracking shouldn't clear outer frame R1-R5 for callbacks\n\nCVE-2026-98034:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark NULL kptr stores precise\n\nCVE-2026-80734:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbtrfs: initialize inode mapping flags for cached inodes\n\nCVE-2026-68399:\n\tIn the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix UAF in sock clone early bailouts\n",
